abstract: >
  Analysis code supporting the study of Kelvin–Helmholtz-driven magnetic
  reconnection observed by the Magnetospheric Multiscale (MMS) mission at
  Earth's distant dawnside magnetopause. The analysis examines 15 current
  sheets with magnetic reconnection signatures observed during an extended
  interval of Kelvin–Helmholtz wave activity on 17–18 June 2020.

keywords:
  - Magnetospheric Multiscale
  - MMS
  - Kelvin-Helmholtz instability
  - magnetic reconnection
  - magnetopause
  - space plasma physics
  - PySPEDAS
  - Python

